fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of main..97ab454 on an isolated snapshot.

Two rounds. Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND with four blockers: the
unconfined public document API still shipping, no version bump for two
breaking changes, a scan that answered empty on a climb through a
missing directory, and three guards that survived their own removal.
All four are closed in 685dbee, 8125027 and 97ab454.

Round two verified the fixes by execution on the new tip. 184 tests
with --all-features, clippy and fmt clean. Five mutations re-run
independently, each caught by a named test. The gate fix was proved by
breaking mcp::Served::ensure_writable: cargo test --workspace exits 0
without --all-features and 101 with it.

The climbs() tiebreaker was attacked with absolute paths, absolute and
relative symlinks out, a dangling symlink out, and paths through a
symlinked component. None carries a '..' component and every one is
refused, because cap-std reports an escape as PermissionDenied whether
or not the target exists.

Accepted as follow-up, not blocking: a hard link inside the store
reaching an outside file, ungated unix-only tests in confined.rs, the
subdirectories/scan disagreement on an internal directory symlink,
mcp::Served holding a PathBuf, and a missed changelog line for
Scan.skipped.
